<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  How xcodebuild turns the archive into an .ipa.

  `flutter build ipa` archives first and then exports, and the export half is
  driven entirely by this file. Without it Flutter writes a default one and the
  method it picks is not the one we want.

  ── teamID ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  2CMZQR34RL is EZBIZI LLC. It is stated here, not left to be inferred, because
  the Mac relay also holds certificates for two OTHER teams — a personal
  Developer ID and an Apple Development identity under different accounts. With
  no team named, xcodebuild picks whichever identity it likes and the archive is
  signed by the wrong entity, which App Store Connect rejects at upload with a
  message about the bundle identifier not matching the team.

  ── method ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  app-store-connect: an archive destined for TestFlight and the App Store. The
  alternatives are for other jobs entirely — `development` installs on
  registered devices, `ad-hoc` on a fixed UDID list, `enterprise` needs a
  programme EzBizi is not in.

  ── uploadSymbols ────────────────────────────────────────────────

  On. dSYMs go up with the build, so a crash report from a tester reads as a
  stack trace rather than as hexadecimal. Flutter's engine symbols are large and
  this makes the upload slower; a crash nobody can read is slower still.

  ── manageAppVersionAndBuildNumber ───────────────────────────────

  Off, deliberately. Left on, Xcode helpfully increments the build number during
  export — and then the number in the .ipa is not the number build-app.sh
  stamped, so the version the app reports on screen and the version App Store
  Connect lists disagree. One number governs every platform (client/VERSION);
  nothing downstream is allowed a second opinion.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>method</key>
    <string>app-store-connect</string>

    <key>teamID</key>
    <string>2CMZQR34RL</string>

    <key>signingStyle</key>
    <string>automatic</string>

    <key>uploadSymbols</key>
    <true/>

    <key>manageAppVersionAndBuildNumber</key>
    <false/>

    <key>destination</key>
    <string>export</string>
</dict>
</plist>
